<title>SWEDEN: SKF sells FlexLink unit for 930 mln SKR.</title>
<headline>SKF sells FlexLink unit for 930 mln SKR.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish rollerbearing manufacturer SKF said on Monday it was selling FlexLink Systems AB to Scandinavian Equity Partners (SEP) for 930 million crowns.</p>
<p>SKF said in a statement that it would retain a 10 percent stake in FlexLink under an agreement with SEP that would take effect from August 31 this year.</p>
</text>
